@RequiresState() is a method decorator used to enforce gameplay state requirements before executing a server-side handler.
It validates the current state flags of the player (such as dead, cuffed, onduty, etc.) and blocks execution if the player does not meet the defined conditions. This allows gameplay rules to be expressed declaratively and kept close to the logic they protect.
The decorator wraps the original method and performs state validation at runtime.

code:
@Controller()
export class InventoryController {

  @RequiresState({ missing: ['dead', 'cuffed'] })
  openInventory(player: Player) {
    // inventory can only be opened if the player is alive and free
  }

  @RequiresState({
    has: ['police_duty'],
    missing: ['dead'],
    errorMessage: 'You must be on duty to access the armory.',
  })
  openArmory(player: Player) {
    // restricted to on-duty police officers
  }
}

